## 1. STRICT RULES & ARCHITECTURE

**1.1 CSS-First Architecture & Zero Inline CSS**
- **No Inline CSS:** The `style="..."` attribute is forbidden anywhere in the HTML. No `<style>` blocks in `index.html` either.
- **Class/ID Selectors Only:** All design properties, layout rules, and states are targeted via class or ID selectors in `style.css`.
- **Minimal HTML Modifications:** HTML stays clean, semantic, and style-agnostic — changing the look must only require editing `style.css`.

**1.2 CSS Variables & Theme Tokens**
- Every color, radius, spacing, shadow, transition, and z-index value must come from `var(--...)`. **No hardcoded hex values outside `:root` / `.dark`.**
- **Contrast Pairing:** Every light background token pairs with a dark text token and vice versa, in both themes. Example fix you must implement: the base `.btn--primary` (`background: var(--color-text); color: #ffffff`) breaks in dark mode — override it under `.dark` so the button inverts (`color: var(--color-bg)`).
- Verify `--color-text-muted` and `--color-accent` meet WCAG AA (≥ 4.5:1 for body text) in both modes; darken/brighten within the theme's grey-neutral mood if they fail. Use `--color-accent` for borders, focus rings, and large text — never as the sole carrier of meaning.

**1.3 Mandatory Dark Mode Support**
- **Implementation:** Define dark tokens under a `.dark` class on `<html>`, plus an `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` fallback scoped to `:root:not(.light):not(.dark)` for no-JS first visits. The X-image pattern and dashed borders must remain clearly visible in dark mode (they adapt automatically via variables — verify it).
- **Theme Switching:** Background and text variables must flip with zero HTML restructuring.
- **Persistence:** Store the user's choice in `localStorage` (key: `lofi-theme`); fall back to `prefers-color-scheme` on first visit. JS always sets an explicit `.light` or `.dark` class. Provide a visible toggle button in the nav using a Google Material icon (`dark_mode` / `light_mode`), with correct `aria-pressed` and `aria-label` state.

**1.4 Flexbox Layout & Mobile-First Alignment**
- Build all layout structures with Flexbox. **Every flex container defaults to `align-items: center`** unless an exception is explicitly justified in a CSS comment.
- **Mobile-friendly first:** Rows convert to columns below ~768px; the nav collapses to a hamburger menu; **horizontal scrolling is forbidden at any viewport width**. Use fluid type via `clamp()` and `width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-6), 1120px)` containers.
- All interactive targets are minimum 44×44px.

**1.5 Framework Default**
- Use **clean vanilla CSS driven by the token system in Section 0** (the theme ships its own component classes — extend them). Tailwind utilities are permitted only if configured to consume these CSS variables; never introduce a second, conflicting token system. Utility usage must map back to generic reusable classes (`.btn`, `.card`, `.input-group`).

**1.6 Typography & Icons (Google Fonts Mandatory)**
- **Text:** Load **Balsamiq Sans** (400, 700, italic) from Google Fonts for `--font-sans` / `--font-display` — it is the authentic Balsamiq hand-drawn typeface. Load **Space Mono** for `--font-mono` (annotation labels, "IMG" tags, prices).
- **Icons:** Use **Google Material Symbols (Outlined)** via the standard `<link>` tag. **Inline SVGs and local icon files are forbidden.**
- All imagery is CSS-generated (X-pattern placeholders) — the page contains **no `<img>` elements**.

