## 3. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

- **Responsive by Default:** Fluid sizing, stacking breakpoints, zero horizontal overflow, `scroll-margin-top` on sections (sticky header), `scroll-behavior: smooth` disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Smooth Animations:** `transition: var(--transition-normal)` on all state changes; every animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
- **Accessibility (a11y):** AA contrast in both modes; semantic HTML5 landmarks (`header`, `main`, `section[aria-labelledby]`, `footer`); one `<h1>`, logical heading hierarchy; a "Skip to content" link; correct ARIA on the theme toggle, mobile menu (`aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, closes on `Esc`), and accordion; `aria-live` regions for form errors, loading, and success feedback; full keyboard operability; state is never communicated by color alone.
- **Mandatory Visual Feedback:** Every click, hover, and submission triggers a visible state change.
- **Decorative placeholders:** Grey placeholder text bars (`.placeholder-line` — `--color-placeholder` background, pill radius, width modifiers) must carry `aria-hidden="true"`.

